  "result": "All three tests pass. The package is implemented in `netgraph/graph.py`.\n\n```\n3 passed in 0.03s\n```\n\n**What was done**\n- Added the missing `Graph` class in `netgraph/graph.py`. Nothing else in the repo needed changing, and `tests/` is untouched.\n- Every public method validates node ids with an explicit range check, so negative ids raise `IndexError` rather than silently wrapping around via Python indexing.\n- Self-loops are stored once and counted once. Duplicate edges are detected before the counter increments, so `edge_count` stays exact.\n- `shortest_path` is a breadth-first search that records parents and reconstructs the path on reaching the target. Same-node queries return a single-element list, and unreachable targets return `None`.\n\n**Approach chosen**\nI chose Approach A, adjacency sets, because the spec's workload is dominated by neighbour iteration and BFS, which are proportional to degree with lists but proportional to n with a matrix. Sets still give O(1) edge lookup and duplicate detection, so the matrix's main advantage is not lost.\n\nChanges are left uncommitted in the working tree since you did not ask for a commit.",
